# `generator-shortcuts`

The repaired source now names three strong canonical-fitting rivals, one for each key of the selected sort order:

1. **`cell_count_first`** — order by occupied cells before bounding-box width;
2. **`height_ascending_on_width_ties`** — when widths tie, put the shorter crop first;
3. **`color_descending_on_dimension_ties`** — when width and height tie, put the larger color first.

All three fit all three usable canonical demonstrations. The canonical examples do not contain the exact width/cell-count inversion or the secondary-key ties needed to distinguish them.

Exact source-bound separators are retained in:

- `counterexamples/cell_count_first.json`;
- `counterexamples/height_tie.json`;
- `counterexamples/color_tie.json`.

Each record pins generator version `2.1.0`, generator SHA-256 `6790a56640ea1cf49ca945e6794781b42dedcda4dc1c8eb72e0cc1c9b2e8a064`, and rule hash `7991026f57da`. The first case makes a width-4 five-cell crop compete with a width-2 six-cell crop. The second makes equal-width crops of heights 3 and 2 compete. The third makes equal 2×4 crops of colors 2 and 8 compete.

`workspace/verify_width_lesson.py --racket` checked the live declarations and all retained cases. Every rival still fits the canonical pairs; every retained input passes `self_check`; each rival has a separator and matching witness; the selected Racket output is valid and equals the independent Python mirror on all three cases; the executed/catalog rule hash matches `7991026f57da`. The retained receipt is `counterexamples/current-shortcut/checks/width-lesson-probe.json`.

**Does the generator emit these cases?** Yes. Every ordinary draw retains a width-vs-cell-count inversion. Three-object draws alternate height-tie and color-tie lessons; four-object draws contain both. The shared semantic gate enumerated the complete four-step schedule and required every hold-one-out query rotation to remain identifiable. A separate bounded stress pass checked 15,360 sliding-window/query rotations without finding a surviving declared rival.
